{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1786928032956285001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"ripening-liberal-tuatara","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":4,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"ca2e1c11cde97ca4e65f9a1fc75744b0bd38aad7edb97063a00e65f640301c36","event_uuid":"e56b75b4-7f81-40a6-9044-a170395dbbf9","position":{"commit_sha":"a7237988f7fe0e19b588fe454ead441054444911","position":"1786924779290617001-e56b75b4-7f81-40a6-9044-a170395dbbf9"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"b43685a2de1bbd3837d0634408d0debd2d7a4bc177a77f4e530e63d018bbf978","event_uuid":"6d97a2c1-d878-4695-a613-197527d830b3","position":{"commit_sha":"8c9486584679ecfaa3fd30af797c9238c2e482a7","position":"1786924829250076001-6d97a2c1-d878-4695-a613-197527d830b3"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"d0b42de7b5037473a40d6b1e81e4fb76f31d5bde43d996613badc53ef7e55ae5","event_uuid":"b17d659f-c55b-4eff-bd00-de5c3fe604a4","position":{"commit_sha":"eca67611f0aa110641cca7a3ffa9fa9afcf046d6","position":"1786924855074048001-b17d659f-c55b-4eff-bd00-de5c3fe604a4"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"fa9e1a5575e01623ea00a307b8684c66129cc9833485312d9441f79d6c6f7d69","event_uuid":"45803415-b082-42b4-b166-4c5021e01564","position":{"commit_sha":"50d070aa82769d4b2c78379b2b645f944228c943","position":"1786924859766287001-45803415-b082-42b4-b166-4c5021e01564"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1786924779290617001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"b17d659f-c55b-4eff-bd00-de5c3fe604a4","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"558e-d9bd-e285-40a1"},{"link_uuid":"45803415-b082-42b4-b166-4c5021e01564","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"2e1b-6517-eb1e-4309"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe approved Pydantic output, bounded-operation, compatibility, and candidate-tracing children establish the replacement behavior [rebar:serge-monotonous-aruanas] [rebar:amoebaean-hemihedral-vervet]. The final change must make that path authoritative for library, CLI, MCP, plan-review, code-review, and completion operations, prove provider-cache behavior, then remove the obsolete manual retry machinery without breaking patch/import seams.\n\n## Approach\nSwitch every structured `PydanticAIRunner` consumer to the new one-operation path through the existing facade. Preserve `ProviderSession`, candidate order, output-mode policy, tool surfaces, timeout/transport limits, provenance, and serialized verdict shapes. Run the complete ticket/test oracle and authorized direct Anthropic plus Bedrock cache canaries before deletion. Once parity and approved deltas pass, remove only the obsolete structured-output attempt scheduler and temporary compatibility delegation; retain deterministic parsing, the stable runner facade, and existing public/re-export paths. Document the new retry layers, shared request budget, complete-or-omit history rule, trace-not-usage candidate semantics, and the reviewed raise-the-limit follow-up policy.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/llm/runner.py`, `src/rebar/llm/structured_run.py`, `src/rebar/llm/agent_call.py` — authoritative call-site cutover and obsolete retry-path removal.\n- `src/rebar/llm/structured.py` — retain pure repair and stop/refusal policy; remove only dead retry integration.\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/`, `src/rebar/llm/code_review/`, and completion runner consumers — compatibility verification and any narrow result projection updates.\n- `docs/llm-framework.md`, `docs/reuse-surface.md` — documented runtime and library contracts.\n- The RP-01 focused runner, structured-output, fallback, usage, failure, cache, plan-review, code-review, and completion suites.\n\n## Testing\n- Run the recovered 38-scenario behavior matrix and all focused historical ticket regressions.\n- Run lean/full import, lint, typecheck, complexity, and module-size gates.\n- Run direct Anthropic and Bedrock same-run retry canaries using environment-provided credentials without printing or persisting secrets; record cache read/write/input counts and complete-versus-omitted wire observations on the ticket.\n- Confirm rollback by temporarily selecting the pre-removal compatibility commit against the same fixtures; no stored data migration is involved.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Library, CLI, MCP, plan-review, code-review, and completion structured calls all use the one-operation Pydantic path through `PydanticAIRunner`; verified by consumer contract tests and a source reference census.\n- [ ] The recovered RP-01 behavior matrix passes with only the approved deltas: shared request exhaustion, bounded output-size retry, complete-or-omit failed response, aggregate successful-run usage, exact causal restoration, and candidate tracing outside usage.\n- [ ] No bespoke structured-output retry scheduler or fresh-Agent output-attempt loop remains; verified by source review and tests that fail if more than one outer Agent run is constructed.\n- [ ] Existing provider fallback eligibility/order, tool limits, timeout/transport ownership, provenance, final artifact policy, and serialized output shapes remain green in their historical regression suites.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] Direct Anthropic and Bedrock canaries pass with secrets absent from output and artifacts; the ticket records timestamp, model ids, request counts, cache read/write/input counts, complete/omit branch, and successful typed result.\n- [ ] `make lint`, `make typecheck`, the focused suite, module-size gate, and complexity ratchet pass with `runner.py` at or below 800 lines and every new module between 100 and 500 lines.\n- [ ] The documented retry-layer and accounting contracts match runtime behavior, including the normal plan-reviewed follow-up to raise the shared allowance if legitimate recovery is starved.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/runner.py","reason":"cut all consumers to the authoritative path"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/structured_run.py","reason":"remove obsolete structured-output attempt scheduling"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/agent_call.py","reason":"remove temporary compatibility delegation"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/structured.py","reason":"retain pure policy while deleting dead retry integration"},{"path":"docs/llm-framework.md","reason":"document retry layers and shared budget"},{"path":"docs/reuse-surface.md","reason":"document the stable runner and accounting contract"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_pydantic_ai_runner.py","reason":"prove final runner cutover"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_structured.py","reason":"retain complete structured-output regression coverage"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_llm_fallback_chain.py","reason":"retain provider fallback behavior"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_usage_log_failed_calls.py","reason":"retain one-row accounting"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","2e1b-6517-eb1e-4309"],["depends_on","558e-d9bd-e285-40a1"],["parent","905d-1287-effc-4a83"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"905d-1287-effc-4a83","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["janitor","rp01","llm","cutover"],"ticket_id":"10a3-7dd0-1b3d-47cc","ticket_type":"story","title":"RP-01 S5 — Cut over runner consumers and remove bespoke structured-output retries","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["e56b75b4-7f81-40a6-9044-a170395dbbf9","6d97a2c1-d878-4695-a613-197527d830b3","b17d659f-c55b-4eff-bd00-de5c3fe604a4","45803415-b082-42b4-b166-4c5021e01564"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786928032956285001,"uuid":"aef1581e-34ce-4655-8a37-ea5f436f7f43"}